<!-- This is an example of how to fill the question-bank.md file, which is part of the configuration for the interview-prep mode
Add here the questions you have received in previous interviews and save it in this folder as question-bank.md
-->

## General ones

- Why should we pick you?
- What's your motivation for this role?
- Why did you apply to this role/company?
- What do you like most about data/software/tech/your field?
- Tell us about something you built/did just out of your own interest, not work related.
- Have you ever worked on something you didn't like or weren't passionate about?
- Do you read about [your field] outside work?
- (In case of changing fields) Why do you want to leave your current field?
- (In case of still being employed) Why do you want to leave your current job?
- Tell us about the accomplishment you're most proud of.
- What impact do you expect to have here? How do you define impact?
- If we asked your colleagues: strengths, weaknesses, three words.
- According to yourself: strengths, weaknesses, three words.
- Would you define yourself as entrepreneurial?
- Do you prefer the business or technical side?
- What skills and background experiences make you ideal for this job?
- What are your expectations for this role?
- What do you do if you have to make a choice but there's scarcity of information?
- Do you modify your way of working under pressure? How?
- Tell us about a challenge you overcame.
- Tell us about one time you helped/mentored a junior colleague.
- Tell us about one time you drove an idea of yours to completion.
- Tell us about one time where you didn't make a deadline.
- Tell us about one time where you proactively fixed an issue affecting your team.
- Tell us about one time when you delivered a high-priority project under a tight deadline.
- Tell us about one time when you built a metric that identified the need for change.
- Have you ever convinced a colleague who disagreed about a shared goal? How?
- Have you ever found a colleague who was difficult to work with? What did you do? How did you solve the situation?
- Have you ever held an unpopular stance with your peers and leader? What did you do?
- Have you ever been unsatisfied with the status quo? How did you proceed?
- Tell us about when you solved a complex problem with a simple solution.
- Have you worked on something to improve your own effectiveness? How did you identify your weakness, how did you tackle it and how it turned out?
- Have you ever identified a clear risk to a commitment? How did you communicate it?
- Have you ever advocated for someone with less influence/power/seniority? How?
- Imagine you can join one of two projects: one that is quite technically standard and straightforward and long, but with huge positive impact on the business; the other is cooler from the technical point of view, more challenging, you might learn more, but its impact is unclear. Which one would you choose and why?

## AAA — Cool Company — Dream Senior Job (Ideal Focus)

- What is your motivation to join The Cool Company in this particular role? (90 seconds)
- What are the skills and background experiences that make you ideal for this role? (90 seconds)
- What are your expectations from this role? (90 seconds)
- Tell us about one time in which you transformed one business idea into a statistical model. How did you do it? What did you consider? (120 seconds)
- Take one statistical approach you have worked with recently and describe its advantages and disadvantages for your use case. (120 seconds)